*.bak_*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data hygiene
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw third-party inputs are NOT redistributed. Keep only the manifest.
# `data/external/*` rather than `data/external/` so the two manifest files can be
# tracked: a bare directory pattern would exclude everything inside it, and a
# negation cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded.
data/external/*
!data/external/SHA256SUMS
!data/external/SOURCES.tsv
!data/external/README.md
data/raw/
# Outputs of the two published-raster patch scripts. They write these next to the rasters
# they read; the checked-in references are FigS1_published.png / FigS3_published.png.
code/figures/ge_si/published/*_reapplied.png
# Transient per-run backups some figure scripts create on their first run.
# `figures/README.md` states the policy — "the `_backup_before_*` directories
# some scripts create on their first run are transient and are not committed" —
# but nothing enforced it, so they showed up as untracked files after any
# `code/run_all.sh`. Stated and enforced are different things.
figures/_backup_before_*/
# SI Fig. S2's recovered generator (script-internal name FigS4). `code/run_all.sh`
# regenerates it into figures/ from 2026-10-05; unlike Fig3-Fig8 its outputs are not part
# of the tracked set (the submitted Fig. S2 raster is a re-draw of what it emits), so the
# build products stay out of version control. The three published medians it must
# reproduce (374 / 632 / 669) are asserted by run_all.sh.
figures/FigS4.png
figures/FigS4.pdf
figures/_numbers_figs4.json
figures/_gen_figs4.txt
# Large archives and alignment/genotype formats belong in Zenodo / figshare /
# iProX, not in git history.
# NOTE: bare `*.gz` is deliberately NOT ignored — the predecessor repository
# tracks small gzipped derived tables such as data/.../*.csv.gz.
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.bam
*.bai
*.cram
*.vcf
*.vcf.gz
*.bgz
*.tbk
*.h5
*.rds
*.RData
